>> On the side note, I had to keep the hacky code e.g. guide_grid_orig <- ggplot2:::guide_grid to be able to display the desired grid style. Is this fixed in 0.91 or is there an alternative way to configure it?
>
> There is a development branch with the new theming system, and I even think it made it to release candidate status recently (search the devel mailing list for a message from Winston Chang). With the new code on this branch you can control the grid lines of x and y independently.
>

Instructions for installing the new version:
  https://github.com/wch/ggplot2/wiki/Installing-the-development-version-of-ggplot2

And you can get rid of just the horizontal or vertical grid lines with
something like this:
  theme(panel.major.x = element_blank(), panel.minor.x = element_blank())

Note that opts() has been replaced by theme() and theme_blank() has
been replaced by element_blank().

If you're interested, here is more information about the new theming system:
  https://github.com/wch/ggplot2/wiki/New-theme-system

-Winston

