Hi,

It looks like the parser fails when a non-ascii character is
represented in position one. For example, this works:

qplot(1, 1, geom="text", label="x >= y", parse=TRUE)

But this does not:
qplot(1, 1, geom="text", label=" >= y", parse=TRUE)
Error in parse(text = lab) : <text>:1:2: unexpected '>='
1:  >=
    ^

Similarly, this works:

qplot(1, 1, geom="text", label="x^2", parse=TRUE)

But this does not:

qplot(1, 1, geom="text", label="^2", parse=TRUE)
Error in parse(text = lab) : <text>:1:1: unexpected '^'
1: ^

If I were you I would probably go with

Svavellabel<-c("0", "600", "5000", "10000", "≥15000")

as Ben suggested.

Best,
Ista

