On Thu, Aug 2, 2012 at 8:35 AM, Dennis Murphy <djm...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I tried playing with this yesterday. I can get the >= 15000 part to
> work alone, but not as part of a character vector. To follow-up on
> Ista's attempt, if you look into the plotmath demo in base R you'll
> eventually come across this trick, which is borrowed from LaTeX:
>
> qplot(1, 1, geom="text", label="phantom(x) >= 15000", parse=TRUE)
>
>>= is a binary operator in plotmath, so it requires two operands. phantom() substitutes equivalent space for the text argument it is given. This works all by its lonesome. Alas, when it's put into a character vector, it falls apart:
>
> lab <- c("0", "600", "5000", "10000", "phantom(x) >= 15000")
> qplot(1, 1) +
>    geom_text(data = pts, aes(x = x, y = y, label = lab), parse = TRUE) +
>    xlim(0.6, 1.4)

