Hi:

You can use the limits = argument of a scale function to expand or
contract the limits. For example, if you do

p + scale_x_reverse(limits = c(20, -5))

just before the print(p) statement at the end, almost all the labeling
becomes visible, but you probably want that to be shaded in pink, so
you'll likely need to make a few adjustments in your code to allow
yourself that extra space.

HTH,
Dennis

